==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|zombiefy}}

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|zombie|fy}}.

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|fictional}} To turn into a [[zombie]] (a member of the [[living dead]] or [[undead]]).
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1994|publisher=Arnold, et al|title=A History of Literature in the Caribbean: Hispanic and Francophone Regions
|passage=She managed to flee the sorcerer who had attempted to '''zombify''' her and enjoyed relative prosperity in Jamaica.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To take control of (a computer) in order to use it covertly and illicitly.
#: {{ux|en|These trojans can '''zombify''' your machine.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|idiomatic}} To [[deprive]] of [[authenticity]] or [[vitality]]; to render someone [[brainless]] or [[unthinking]].
#* {{quote-song
|en
|year=2022
|title='''Zombified'''
|artist=Falling in Reverse
|album=Neon Zombie
|passage='''Zombified''' by the lies they said, we’ve become the walking dead.}}

